Aim To create a forensically sound, bit-for-bit copy of a storage device using FTK Image or Guy mager. To verify the imager integrity by comparing the SHA-256 hash volve of the original source and the 
final image file.

Theory:
> Forensic Imaging

جاForensic sound

>Image Formats:
      Row/DD(dd,img)

>Integrity & Hoshing

>Chain of custody

Methodology:

1. Prepare: Connect source device to write blocker.

2. Select source file Create Disk Image Select the source drive

3. Configure: Click Add Choose image type [Raw or fai] Enter case details

             →Select destination folder

4. Verily: Click the box [verify image after they are created] Click [Start]

5. Documentation: After Completion, note SHA-256 hash from the verification window in your chain of Custody log

Future Scope:

The foundation skill enables further forensic analysis Such as file recovery and artifact examination. Futhore work con include imaging volatile memory [Ram] or acquiring evidence from cloud storage environment
